Date: Fri, 31 Oct 2025 15:31:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 41/46] Add Taproot address support to RPC and address encoding
 (#29)

Fixes issue where Taproot addresses (type 2 XAddress) were rejected as
"Invalid address" by getaddressinfo and other RPC calls.

Changes:
- Add TaprootDestination type to CTxDestination variant
- Update ExtractDestination to extract Taproot commitment as destination
- Update GetScriptForDestination to generate Taproot scripts
- Add TAPROOT (type 2) to XAddress AddressType enum
- Update XAddress encoder/parser to handle 33-byte Taproot commitments
- Update RPC address description visitors for Taproot destinations
- CashAddr returns empty string for Taproot (format unsupported)

Before this change, Taproot scripts were recognized but couldn't be
converted to destinations, preventing address validation and wallet
operations. Now Taproot addresses decode properly and work with RPC
commands like getaddressinfo and validateaddress.

Also, some additional commits to bugfix missing Taproot handlers to
visitor classes and Lotus-QT crashing when decoding Taproot
addresses.
